/-!
# Chern classes of a tensor product of finite locally free modules, in the ring of total classes

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project, let `X` be locally of
finite type over `S` and let `ℰ` and `ℱ` be finite locally free `𝒪_X`-modules of ranks `r` and
`s`. [Stacks, Tag 0FA6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FA6) is the pair of identities

  `c₁(ℰ ⊗ ℱ) = r·c₁(ℱ) + s·c₁(ℰ)`,

  `c₂(ℰ ⊗ ℱ) = r·c₂(ℱ) + s·c₂(ℰ) + C(r,2)·c₁(ℱ)² + (r·s − 1)·c₁(ℱ)·c₁(ℰ) + C(s,2)·c₁(ℰ)²`,

in `A^*(X)`, together with the remark "and so on", which is not a precise assertion and for which
nothing is claimed. Both identities are proved here for every `r` and `s`, rank zero included,
for the Chern classes `c_i(ℰ) ∈ A^i(X)` of [Stacks, Tag 0B7H]. They are stated in the ring
`Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass C sX` of total Chow cohomology classes, the product `∏_p A^p(X)` with
the products `A^i(X) × A^j(X) ⟶ A^{i+j}(X)` of [Stacks, Tag 0B75]: `c_i(ℰ)` is the degree-`i`
part `TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sX ℰ r)` of the total Chern class, which is
zero for `i > r`, and `ℰ ⊗ ℱ` is the tensor product `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` of
`𝒪_X`-modules, of rank `r·s` by `Stacks.Chow.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor`. Read on the Chow
groups of `X` the same identities hold in the ring of graded cap families on which the total
Chern class `Stacks.Chow.GenuineChern.chernFamily` lives
(`Stacks.Chow.tensorChernRelations_chernFamily`).

## The proof

The source reduces to bundles with filtrations by invertible modules and omits the formal
computation. The proof here is the same splitting argument, organised as an induction on the rank
`s` of `ℱ`, one invertible quotient at a time, so that no complete flag and no symmetric-function
identity is needed. The six classes `c₁, c₂` of `ℰ`, `ℱ`, `ℰ ⊗ ℱ` satisfy the relations
`Stacks.Chow.TensorChernRelations r s` of the statement.

* In rank `s = 0` the module `ℱ` and the tensor product vanish, so all their Chern classes but
  `c_0 = 1` do.
* For `s = m + 1`, a total class is determined by its operations on the test schemes
  `g : T ⟶ X` (`Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass.ext_op`), and pullback commutes with tensor products,
  so it suffices to prove the relations for the graded cap families of `g^*ℰ`, `g^*ℱ` on `T`.
  There one passes to the projective bundle `π : P = 𝐏(g^*ℱ) ⟶ T`, where the tautological
  sequence `0 ⟶ 𝒦 ⟶ π^*ℱ ⟶ 𝒪(1) ⟶ 0` has `𝒦` of rank `m`. Since `𝒪(1)` is flat, tensoring
  with `π^*ℰ` keeps it exact ([Stacks, Tag 03EX]):
  `0 ⟶ π^*ℰ ⊗ 𝒦 ⟶ π^*ℰ ⊗ π^*ℱ ⟶ π^*ℰ ⊗ 𝒪(1) ⟶ 0`. The Whitney formula
  ([Stacks, Tag 02UI], `Stacks.Chow.totalChern_eq_mul_of_shortExact`) applied to both
  sequences, the twist formula `c(π^*ℰ ⊗ 𝒪(1)) = T_{r,c₁(𝒪(1))}(c(π^*ℰ))` of
  [Stacks, Tag 02UD] (`Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass.totalChern_sheafTensor`) and the relations for
  `π^*ℰ ⊗ 𝒦`, given by induction, yield the relations on `P` after a computation in the
  commutative ring generated by the Chern classes (`Stacks.Chow.tensorChernRelations_succ`; the
  Chern classes commute by [Stacks, Tag 02UA]). The relations descend to `T` because `π^*` is
  injective on Chow groups (the top half of [Stacks, Tag 02TW]) and carries the Chern class cap
  products of a module to those of its pullback ([Stacks, Tag 02U8]).

The coefficient `r·s − 1` of the cross term arises in this induction as the sum of the
coefficient `r·m − 1` of the induction hypothesis and the contribution `r` of the twist.

The operator ring of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SplittingPrinciple.TensorChernClasses`, in which the
identities of Stacks 0FA6 are read componentwise on cap products against filtrations with
invertible quotients, is not used here; this module proves the identities themselves.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.TensorChernRelations` — the two relations of Stacks 0FA6 among elements
  `c₁, c₂` of a ring.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.tensorChernRelations_succ` — the computation of the inductive step.
* `Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass.homPart_twist` — the homogeneous parts of a twist.
* `Stacks.Chow.tensorChernRelations_totalChern` — the two relations, by induction on the rank.
* `Stacks.Chow.totalChern_sheafTensor_degree_one` — **Stacks 0FA6**, the first displayed identity.
* `Stacks.Chow.totalChern_sheafTensor_degree_two` — **Stacks 0FA6**, the second displayed identity.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FA6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FA6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B7H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B7H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B75](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B75)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02U8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02U8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02TW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02TW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03EX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03EX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02U5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02U5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02TJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02TJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02TI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02TI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02SP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02SP)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Finset

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Chow

open CategoryTheory.Limits

/-! ### The relations of Stacks 0FA6 in a ring -/

section Relations

variable {R : Type*} [Ring R]

/-- **The relations of Stacks 0FA6** among elements `e₁, e₂`, `f₁, f₂` and `t₁, t₂` of a ring,
standing for the first two Chern classes of modules `ℰ` of rank `r`, `ℱ` of rank `s` and
`ℰ ⊗ ℱ`:

  `t₁ = r·f₁ + s·e₁`,  `t₂ = r·f₂ + s·e₂ + C(r,2)·f₁² + (r·s − 1)·f₁·e₁ + C(s,2)·e₁²`. -/
def TensorChernRelations (r s : ℕ) (e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ : R) : Prop :=
  t₁ = (r : ℤ) • f₁ + (s : ℤ) • e₁ ∧
    t₂ = (r : ℤ) • f₂ + (s : ℤ) • e₂ + (r.choose 2 : ℤ) • f₁ ^ 2 +
      ((r : ℤ) * s - 1) • (f₁ * e₁) + (s.choose 2 : ℤ) • e₁ ^ 2

/-- The relations are preserved by ring homomorphisms. -/
theorem TensorChernRelations.map {R' : Type*} [Ring R'] (φ : R →+* R') {r s : ℕ}
    {e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ : R} (h : TensorChernRelations r s e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂) :
    TensorChernRelations r s (φ e₁) (φ e₂) (φ f₁) (φ f₂) (φ t₁) (φ t₂) := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂⟩ := h
  exact ⟨by rw [h₁, map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul],
    by simp only [h₂, map_add, map_zsmul, map_mul, map_pow]⟩

/-- `2·C(r,2) = r·(r − 1)`, in the integers. -/
private theorem natCast_choose_two_mul_two (r : ℕ) :
    ((r.choose 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) * 2 = r * ((r : ℤ) - 1) := by
  induction r with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [Nat.choose_succ_succ', Nat.choose_one_right]
    push_cast
    linear_combination ih

/-- **The computation of the inductive step.** In a commutative ring, let `e₁, e₂` be the Chern
classes of `ℰ` of rank `r`, let `0 ⟶ 𝒦 ⟶ ℱ ⟶ ℒ ⟶ 0` be exact with `𝒦` of rank `m` and `ℒ`
invertible, and write `a_i`, `f_i`, `x = c₁(ℒ)` for the Chern classes of `𝒦`, `ℱ`, `ℒ` and
`u_i`, `w_i`, `t_i` for those of `ℰ ⊗ 𝒦`, `ℰ ⊗ ℒ`, `ℰ ⊗ ℱ`. If the relations hold for `ℰ` and
`𝒦`, then the Whitney formulas `f = a·(1 + x)` and `t = u·w` in degrees one and two and the twist
formula `w₁ = e₁ + r·x`, `w₂ = e₂ + (r − 1)·e₁·x + C(r,2)·x²` give the relations for `ℰ` and
`ℱ`. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_succ {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (r m : ℕ)
    {e₁ e₂ a₁ a₂ x f₁ f₂ u₁ u₂ w₁ w₂ t₁ t₂ : A}
    (hu : TensorChernRelations r m e₁ e₂ a₁ a₂ u₁ u₂)
    (hf₁ : f₁ = a₁ + x) (hf₂ : f₂ = a₂ + a₁ * x)
    (hw₁ : w₁ = e₁ + (r : ℤ) • x)
    (hw₂ : w₂ = e₂ + ((r : ℤ) - 1) • (e₁ * x) + (r.choose 2 : ℤ) • x ^ 2)
    (ht₁ : t₁ = u₁ + w₁) (ht₂ : t₂ = u₂ + u₁ * w₁ + w₂) :
    TensorChernRelations r (m + 1) e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ := by
  obtain ⟨hu₁, hu₂⟩ := hu
  have hr : ((r.choose 2 : ℕ) : A) * 2 = r * ((r : A) - 1) := by
    exact_mod_cast congrArg (Int.cast : ℤ → A) (natCast_choose_two_mul_two r)
  have hm : (((m + 1).choose 2 : ℕ) : A) = (m.choose 2 : ℕ) + m := by
    rw [Nat.choose_succ_succ', Nat.choose_one_right]
    push_cast
    ring
  subst ht₁ ht₂ hw₁ hw₂ hf₁ hf₂ hu₁ hu₂
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩ <;>
    simp only [zsmul_eq_mul, Int.cast_add, Int.cast_sub, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_one,
      Int.cast_natCast, Nat.cast_add, Nat.cast_one]
  · ring
  · linear_combination (-(a₁ * x)) * hr - e₁ ^ 2 * hm

/-- The relations can be checked after an injective ring homomorphism. -/
theorem TensorChernRelations.of_map_injective {R' : Type*} [Ring R'] (φ : R →+* R')
    (hφ : Function.Injective φ) {r s : ℕ} {e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ : R}
    (h : TensorChernRelations r s (φ e₁) (φ e₂) (φ f₁) (φ f₂) (φ t₁) (φ t₂)) :
    TensorChernRelations r s e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂⟩ := h
  exact ⟨hφ (by rw [h₁, map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul]),
    hφ (by simp only [h₂, map_add, map_zsmul, map_mul, map_pow])⟩

/-- **Descent of the relations along an injective intertwiner.** If `pull` is injective in every
degree and carries six graded cap families to six others satisfying the relations, the first six
satisfy them as well. -/
theorem TensorChernRelations.of_intertwines {G H : ℤ → Type v} [∀ k, AddCommGroup (G k)]
    [∀ k, AddCommGroup (H k)] {d : ℤ} (pull : ∀ k : ℤ, G k →+ H (k + d))
    (hinj : ∀ k : ℤ, Function.Injective (pull k)) {r s : ℕ}
    {e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ : GradedCapFamily G} {e₁' e₂' f₁' f₂' t₁' t₂' : GradedCapFamily H}
    (he₁ : Intertwines pull e₁ e₁') (he₂ : Intertwines pull e₂ e₂')
    (hf₁ : Intertwines pull f₁ f₁') (hf₂ : Intertwines pull f₂ f₂')
    (ht₁ : Intertwines pull t₁ t₁') (ht₂ : Intertwines pull t₂ t₂')
    (h : TensorChernRelations r s e₁' e₂' f₁' f₂' t₁' t₂') :
    TensorChernRelations r s e₁ e₂ f₁ f₂ t₁ t₂ := by
  have key : ∀ {a b : GradedCapFamily G} {a' : GradedCapFamily H}, Intertwines pull a a' →
      Intertwines pull b a' → a = b := fun ha hb => funext fun k => funext fun i =>
    AddMonoidHom.ext fun x => hinj _ (by rw [ha k i x, hb k i x])
  have hsq : ∀ {a : GradedCapFamily G} {a' : GradedCapFamily H}, Intertwines pull a a' →
      Intertwines pull (a ^ 2) (a' ^ 2) := fun ha => by
    rw [pow_two, pow_two]
    exact Intertwines.mul ha ha
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂⟩ := h
  rw [h₁] at ht₁
  rw [h₂] at ht₂
  refine ⟨key ht₁ (Intertwines.add (Intertwines.zsmul hf₁ _) (Intertwines.zsmul he₁ _)),
    key ht₂ ?_⟩
  refine Intertwines.add (Intertwines.add (Intertwines.add (Intertwines.add
    (Intertwines.zsmul hf₂ _) (Intertwines.zsmul he₂ _)) (Intertwines.zsmul (hsq hf₁) _))
    (Intertwines.zsmul (Intertwines.mul hf₁ he₁) _)) (Intertwines.zsmul (hsq he₁) _)

end Relations

/-! ### Homogeneous parts of twists -/

namespace TotalChowClass

variable {C : ChowSituation.{u}} {Y : Scheme.{u}} {sY : Y ⟶ C.S} [LocallyOfFiniteType sY]

/-- The degree-`m` part of a series is the degree-`m` part of its `m`-th term. -/
theorem homPart_series (f : ℕ → TotalChowClass C sY) (m : ℕ) :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent m (series f) = TotalChowClass.homComponent m (f m) :=
  ext fun p => by
    rw [TotalChowClass.homComponent_apply, TotalChowClass.homComponent_apply]
    split_ifs with hp
    · subst hp
      rfl
    · rfl

/-- The `j`-th power of a class of degree `1` has degree `j`. -/
theorem IsHomogeneous.pow {x : TotalChowClass C sY} (hx : x.IsHomogeneous 1) (j : ℕ) :
    (x ^ j).IsHomogeneous j := by
  induction j with
  | zero => rw [pow_zero]; exact isHomogeneous_one
  | succ j ih => rw [pow_succ]; exact ih.mul hx

/-- **The homogeneous parts of a twist**: for `x` of degree `1`, the degree-`m` part of
`T_{r,x}(c)` is `∑_{j ≤ m} binom(r - m + j, j) c_{m-j} x^j`. -/
theorem homPart_twist {x : TotalChowClass C sY} (hx : x.IsHomogeneous 1) (r : ℤ)
    (c : TotalChowClass C sY) (m : ℕ) :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent m (twist r x c) = ∑ j ∈ range (m + 1),
      Ring.choose (r - m + j) j • (TotalChowClass.homComponent (m - j) c * x ^ j) := by
  rw [twist_apply, homPart_series]
  refine IsHomogeneous.homComponent_self (IsHomogeneous.sum fun j hj => ?_)
  have hjm : j ≤ m := Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (mem_range.mp hj)
  have h := ((TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent (m - j) c).mul (hx.pow j)).zsmul
    (Ring.choose (r - m + j) j)
  rwa [Nat.sub_add_cancel hjm] at h

end TotalChowClass

open TotalChowClass

/-! ### The first two Chern classes in a short exact sequence and in a twist -/

section TotalChern

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- Above the rank the Chern classes vanish: `c_i(ℰ) = 0` for `i > r`. -/
theorem homPart_totalChern_of_lt (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] {i : ℕ}
    (hi : r < i) : TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sX E r) = 0 :=
  TotalChowClass.ext fun p => by
    rw [TotalChowClass.homComponent_apply]
    split_ifs with hp
    · subst hp
      exact totalChern_apply_of_lt C sX E r hi
    · rfl

/-- The degree-one part of a product of two total Chern classes:
`(c(ℰ) c(ℱ))₁ = c₁(ℰ) + c₁(ℱ)`. -/
theorem homPart_one_mul_totalChern (E F : X.Modules) (r s : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s] :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r * totalChern C sX F s) =
      TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) +
        TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s) := by
  simp [TotalChowClass.homComponent_mul_sum, sum_range_succ, homPart_zero_totalChern]

/-- The degree-two part of a product of two total Chern classes:
`(c(ℰ) c(ℱ))₂ = c₂(ℰ) + c₁(ℰ) c₁(ℱ) + c₂(ℱ)`. -/
theorem homPart_two_mul_totalChern (E F : X.Modules) (r s : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s] :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r * totalChern C sX F s) =
      TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r) +
        TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) *
          TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s) +
        TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX F s) := by
  simp [TotalChowClass.homComponent_mul_sum, sum_range_succ, homPart_zero_totalChern, add_assoc]

/-- **Stacks 02UD in degree one**: `c₁(ℰ ⊗ ℒ) = c₁(ℰ) + r·c₁(ℒ)` for `ℰ` of rank `r` and `ℒ`
invertible. -/
theorem homPart_one_totalChern_sheafTensor (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L] :
    letI := isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible L
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf)
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj L) r :=
      GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_sheafTensor E r L
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 1
        (totalChern C sX (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj L) r) =
      TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) +
        (r : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX L 1) := by
  rw [totalChern_sheafTensor, homPart_twist (isHomogeneous_firstChernTotal C sX L),
    ← firstChernTotal_eq_homComponent_totalChern]
  simp [sum_range_succ, homPart_zero_totalChern]

/-- **Stacks 02UD in degree two**: `c₂(ℰ ⊗ ℒ) = c₂(ℰ) + (r − 1)·c₁(ℰ)·c₁(ℒ) + C(r,2)·c₁(ℒ)²`
for `ℰ` of rank `r` and `ℒ` invertible. -/
theorem homPart_two_totalChern_sheafTensor (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L] :
    letI := isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible L
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf)
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj L) r :=
      GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_sheafTensor E r L
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 2
        (totalChern C sX (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj L) r) =
      TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r) +
        ((r : ℤ) - 1) • (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) *
          TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX L 1)) +
        (r.choose 2 : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX L 1) ^ 2 := by
  rw [totalChern_sheafTensor, homPart_twist (isHomogeneous_firstChernTotal C sX L),
    ← firstChernTotal_eq_homComponent_totalChern]
  simp [sum_range_succ, homPart_zero_totalChern, Ring.choose_natCast,
    show (r : ℤ) - 2 + 1 = r - 1 by ring]

end TotalChern

open Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor (sheafTensor)

/-! ### The relations in rank zero, and along an extension by an invertible module -/

section Step

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- **The relations in rank zero**: for `ℱ` of rank `0` all Chern classes of `ℱ` and of `ℰ ⊗ ℱ`
in positive degree vanish. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_rank_zero (E F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [hE : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F 0] :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    TensorChernRelations r 0 (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F 0))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX F 0))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1
        (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * 0)))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2
        (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * 0))) := by
  let : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
      isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
  have hT : totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * 0) = 1 :=
    totalChern_eq_one_of_rank_eq_zero C sX _ (r * 0) (Nat.mul_zero r)
  simp only [totalChern_of_rank_zero C sX F, hT]
  have h₁ : TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (1 : TotalChowClass C sX) = 0 :=
    TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous.homPart_of_ne isHomogeneous_one one_ne_zero
  have h₂ : TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (1 : TotalChowClass C sX) = 0 :=
    TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous.homPart_of_ne isHomogeneous_one two_ne_zero
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩ <;> simp [h₁, h₂]

/-- **The inductive step on the projective bundle.** Let `0 ⟶ 𝒦 ⟶ ℱ ⟶ ℒ ⟶ 0` be exact with `𝒦`
of rank `m` and `ℒ` invertible. If the relations hold for `ℰ` and `𝒦`, they hold for `ℰ` and
`ℱ`: tensoring with `ℰ` keeps the sequence exact because `ℒ` is flat (Stacks 03EX), and the
Whitney formula (Stacks 02UI) for both sequences and the twist formula (Stacks 02UD) for
`ℰ ⊗ ℒ` reduce the claim to `Stacks.Chow.tensorChernRelations_succ`, in the commutative ring
`Stacks.Chow.chernRing` of Chern classes. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_shortExact (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [hE : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    (S : ShortComplex X.Modules) (hS : S.ShortExact) (m : ℕ)
    [h₁ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₁ m]
    [h₂ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₂ (m + 1)]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property S.X₃]
    (h : letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
             (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
             isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE h₁
      TensorChernRelations r m (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX S.X₁ m))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX S.X₁ m))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1
          (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₁) (r * m)))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2
          (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₁) (r * m)))) :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE h₂
    TensorChernRelations r (m + 1) (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX S.X₂ (m + 1)))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX S.X₂ (m + 1)))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1
        (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * (m + 1))))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2
        (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * (m + 1)))) := by
  have h₃ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₃ 1 :=
    isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible S.X₃
  obtain ⟨w, hT⟩ : ∃ w : ((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).map S.f ≫
      ((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).map S.g = 0,
      (ShortComplex.mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).map S.f)
        (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).map S.g) w).ShortExact :=
    ⟨_, Stacks.Sheaves.ChangeOfRings.shortExact_map_sheafTensorObj X.sheaf E S hS
      (isFlat_of_isInvertible S.X₃)⟩
  have hT₁ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₁) (r * m) :=
    isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE h₁
  have hT₃ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₃) (r * 1) :=
    isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE h₃
  have hT₃' : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₃) r :=
    GenuineChern.rank_of_iso (Iso.refl _) (Nat.mul_one r) hT₃
  have hT₂ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * (m + 1)) :=
    isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE h₂
  have hW₁ := totalChern_eq_mul_of_shortExact C sX S hS m 1
  have hW₂ := totalChern_eq_mul_of_shortExact C sX _ hT (r * m) (r * 1)
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * m + r * 1) :=
    GenuineChern.rank_of_iso (Iso.refl _) (by ring) hT₂
  have hmid : totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * (m + 1)) =
      totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₁) (r * m) *
        totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₃) r :=
    (totalChern_congr C sX (Iso.refl _) (by ring)).trans (hW₂.trans
      (congrArg _ (totalChern_congr C sX (Iso.refl _) (Nat.mul_one r))))
  let mk : ∀ (M : X.Modules) (n : ℕ)
      [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} M n] (i : ℕ),
      chernRing C sX := fun M n _ i =>
    ⟨_, Subring.subset_closure (homPart_totalChern_mem_chernSet C sX M n i)⟩
  let ι := (chernRing C sX).subtype
  have key := tensorChernRelations_succ (A := chernRing C sX) r m
    (e₁ := mk E r 1) (e₂ := mk E r 2) (a₁ := mk S.X₁ m 1) (a₂ := mk S.X₁ m 2)
    (x := mk S.X₃ 1 1) (f₁ := mk S.X₂ (m + 1) 1) (f₂ := mk S.X₂ (m + 1) 2)
    (u₁ := mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₁) (r * m) 1)
    (u₂ := mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₁) (r * m) 2)
    (w₁ := mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₃) r 1)
    (w₂ := mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₃) r 2)
    (t₁ := mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * (m + 1)) 1)
    (t₂ := mk (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj S.X₂) (r * (m + 1)) 2)
    (TensorChernRelations.of_map_injective ι Subtype.val_injective h)
    (Subtype.ext ((congrArg (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1) hW₁).trans
      (homPart_one_mul_totalChern C sX _ _ m 1)))
    (Subtype.ext ((congrArg (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2) hW₁).trans
      ((homPart_two_mul_totalChern C sX _ _ m 1).trans (by
        rw [homPart_totalChern_of_lt C sX S.X₃ 1 one_lt_two, add_zero]; rfl))))
    (Subtype.ext (homPart_one_totalChern_sheafTensor C sX E r S.X₃))
    (Subtype.ext (homPart_two_totalChern_sheafTensor C sX E r S.X₃))
    (Subtype.ext ((congrArg (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1) hmid).trans
      (homPart_one_mul_totalChern C sX _ _ _ _)))
    (Subtype.ext ((congrArg (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2) hmid).trans
      (homPart_two_mul_totalChern C sX _ _ _ _)))
  exact key.map ι

end Step

/-! ### From total classes to cap products and back, and descent along the bundle -/

section Descent

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u})

/-- **From total classes to cap products.** If the relations hold among the total Chern classes
of `ℰ`, `ℱ`, `𝒯` on `P`, they hold among their Chern class cap products on the Chow groups of
`P`: these are the operations of the total classes on the test scheme `𝟙 P`. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_chernFamily_of_totalChern {P : Scheme.{u}} (sP : P ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sP] (E F T : P.Modules) (r s t : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} T t]
    (h : TensorChernRelations r s (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sP E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sP E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sP F s))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sP F s))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sP T t))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sP T t))) :
    TensorChernRelations r s (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP E r))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP E r))
      (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP F s))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP F s))
      (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP T t))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP T t)) := by
  have h' := h.map (opRingHom (𝟙 P))
  have hop : ∀ (M : P.Modules) (n : ℕ)
      [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} M n] (i : ℕ),
      opRingHom (𝟙 P) (TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sP M n)) =
        homComponent i (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (𝟙 P ≫ sP) M n) := fun M n _ i => by
    let := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank M n (𝟙 P)
    rw [opRingHom_apply, TotalChowClass.op_homComponent, op_totalChern,
      GenuineChern.chernFamily_congr C _ M n ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackId P).app M) rfl]
  rw [hop E r 1, hop E r 2, hop F s 1, hop F s 2, hop T t 1, hop T t 2] at h'
  have key : ∀ (q : P ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType q], q = sP →
      TensorChernRelations r s (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q E r))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q E r))
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q F s))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q F s))
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q T t))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q T t)) →
      TensorChernRelations r s (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP E r))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP E r))
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP F s))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP F s))
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP T t))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sP T t)) := by
    rintro q _ rfl hq
    exact hq
  exact key _ (Category.id_comp sP) h'

/-- **From cap products to total classes.** If the relations hold among the Chern class cap
products of `g^*ℰ`, `g^*ℱ`, `g^*𝒯` on every test scheme `g : Y ⟶ X`, they hold among the total
Chern classes of `ℰ`, `ℱ`, `𝒯`, a total class being determined by its operations. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_op {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (E F T : X.Modules) (r s t : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} T t]
    (h : ∀ {Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) [LocallyOfFiniteType g],
      letI := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank E r g
      letI := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank F s g
      letI := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank T t g
      TensorChernRelations r s
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj E) r))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj E) r))
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F) s))
        (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F) s))
        (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj T) t))
        (homComponent 2
          (GenuineChern.chernFamily C (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj T) t))) :
    TensorChernRelations r s (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX F s))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX T t))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX T t)) := by
  refine ⟨ext_op fun g _ => ?_, ext_op fun g _ => ?_⟩ <;>
    simp only [TotalChowClass.op_add, TotalChowClass.op_zsmul, TotalChowClass.op_pow,
      TotalChowClass.op_mul, TotalChowClass.op_homComponent, op_totalChern]
  · exact (h g).1
  · exact (h g).2

/-- **The inductive step, descended.** Granted the relations for every module of rank `r` and
every module of rank `m` on every scheme, they hold for the Chern class cap products of `ℰ` of
rank `r` and `ℱ` of rank `m + 1`. On the projective bundle `π : 𝐏(ℱ) ⟶ T` the tautological
sequence `0 ⟶ 𝒦 ⟶ π^*ℱ ⟶ 𝒪(1) ⟶ 0` has `𝒦` of rank `m`, so the relations hold for `π^*ℰ`
and `π^*ℱ` by `Stacks.Chow.tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_shortExact`; they descend along
`π^*`, which is injective on Chow groups (the top half of Stacks 02TW) and carries the Chern
class cap products of a module to those of its pullback (Stacks 02U8), with
`π^*(ℰ ⊗ ℱ) ≅ π^*ℰ ⊗ π^*ℱ`. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_chernFamily_succ (r m : ℕ)
    (ih : ∀ {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (E F : X.Modules)
      [hE : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
      [hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F m],
      letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
          (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
          isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
      TensorChernRelations r m (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F m))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX F m))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1
          (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * m)))
        (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2
          (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * m))))
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (q : T ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType q] (E F : T.Modules)
    [hE : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F (m + 1)] :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := T.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    TensorChernRelations r (m + 1) (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q E r))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q E r))
      (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q F (m + 1)))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q F (m + 1)))
      (homComponent 1
        (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q (((sheafTensor T.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * (m + 1))))
      (homComponent 2
        (GenuineChern.chernFamily C q (((sheafTensor T.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * (m + 1)))) := by
  let : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := T.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
      isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} F :=
    GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFree_of_rank F (m + 1)
  have := GenuineChern.flat_bundleProj F m
  have := GenuineChern.locallyOfFiniteType_bundleProj F m
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.isQuasicoherent_of_isFiniteLocallyFree F
  have hd := GenuineChern.relativeDimension_bundleProj F m
  -- the tautological sequence `0 ⟶ 𝒦 ⟶ π^*ℱ ⟶ 𝒪(1) ⟶ 0` on the projective bundle of `ℱ`
  let τ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleProj F)).obj F ⟶ bundleTwist F :=
    Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.tautologicalMap F (bundlePieces F)
  have hτ : Epi τ := Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.epi_tautologicalMap F (bundlePieces F)
  have hE' : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleProj F)).obj E) r :=
    GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_pullback _ E r
  have hF' : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleProj F)).obj F) (m + 1) :=
    GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_pullback _ F (m + 1)
  have hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (bundleTwist F) 1 :=
    isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible _
  have hK : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (kernel τ) m :=
    GenuineChern.rank_of_iso (Iso.refl _) (by omega)
      (Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_kernel_of_epi τ hτ (m + 1) 1
        hF' hL)
  let S : ShortComplex (bundle F).Modules := ShortComplex.mk (kernel.ι τ) τ (kernel.condition τ)
  have hS : S.ShortExact := { exact := ShortComplex.exact_kernel τ }
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₁ m := hK
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₂ (m + 1) := hF'
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (bundle F).sheaf.obj
      (bundle F).ringCatSheaf.property S.X₃ := isInvertible_bundleTwist F
  -- the relations on the bundle, by Stacks 02UI, Stacks 02UD and the induction hypothesis
  have hP := tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_shortExact C (bundleProj F ≫ q)
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (bundleProj F)).obj E) r S hS m (ih _ _ _)
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := (bundle F).ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
      isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE' hF'
  have hP' := tensorChernRelations_chernFamily_of_totalChern C (bundleProj F ≫ q) _ _ _ r (m + 1)
    (r * (m + 1)) hP
  -- descent along `π^*`, injective by Stacks 02TW and compatible with `c` by Stacks 02U8
  have iE := GenuineChern.intertwines_chernFamily C q E r _ (bundleProj F) rfl _ hd _ (Iso.refl _)
  have iF := GenuineChern.intertwines_chernFamily C q F (m + 1) _ (bundleProj F) rfl _ hd _
    (Iso.refl _)
  have iT := GenuineChern.intertwines_chernFamily C q _ (r * (m + 1)) _ (bundleProj F) rfl _ hd _
    (sheafTensorPullbackIso (bundleProj F) E F).symm
  exact TensorChernRelations.of_intertwines
    (fun k => flatPullbackChow C (bundleProj F ≫ q) q (bundleProj F) rfl (m + 1 - 1) hd k
      (flatPullbackFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence_general C _ q _ rfl _ hd k))
    (fun k => GenuineChern.pullback_injective q F (GenuineChern.topHalf C) m k)
    (iE.homComponent 1) (iE.homComponent 2) (iF.homComponent 1) (iF.homComponent 2)
    (iT.homComponent 1) (iT.homComponent 2)
    hP'

/-- **The relations of Stacks 0FA6 for total Chern classes**, by induction on the rank of `ℱ`. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_totalChern (r s : ℕ) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (E F : X.Modules)
    [hE : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    [hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s] :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    TensorChernRelations r s (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX F s))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1
        (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * s)))
      (TotalChowClass.homComponent 2
        (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * s))) := by
  induction s generalizing X with
  | zero => exact tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_rank_zero C sX E F r
  | succ m ih =>
    let : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    refine tensorChernRelations_totalChern_of_op C sX E F _ r (m + 1) (r * (m + 1))
      fun {Y} g _ => ?_
    let hE' := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank E r g
    let hF' := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank F (m + 1) g
    let := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * (m + 1)) g
    let : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := Y.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE' hF'
    have h := tensorChernRelations_chernFamily_succ C r m (fun sX _ E F _ _ => ih sX E F)
      (g ≫ sX) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj E) ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F)
    have hT := GenuineChern.chernFamily_congr C (g ≫ sX) _ (r * (m + 1))
      (sheafTensorPullbackIso g E F) rfl
    exact ⟨(congrArg (homComponent 1) hT).trans h.1, (congrArg (homComponent 2) hT).trans h.2⟩

end Descent

/-! ### Stacks 0FA6 -/

section Main

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]
  (E F : X.Modules) (r s : ℕ)
  [hE : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
  [hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s]

/-- **The relations of Stacks 0FA6 for the Chern class cap products**: in the ring of graded cap
families on the Chow groups of `X`, the homogeneous components of index `1` and `2` of the total
Chern classes `Stacks.Chow.GenuineChern.chernFamily` of `ℰ`, `ℱ` and `ℰ ⊗ ℱ` satisfy the two
identities of Stacks 0FA6. Componentwise, for every `α ∈ A_k(X)`,
`c₁(ℰ ⊗ ℱ) ∩ α = r·(c₁(ℱ) ∩ α) + s·(c₁(ℰ) ∩ α)`, and similarly in degree two with
`c₁(ℱ)² ∩ α = c₁(ℱ) ∩ (c₁(ℱ) ∩ α)` and `c₁(ℱ)c₁(ℰ) ∩ α = c₁(ℱ) ∩ (c₁(ℰ) ∩ α)`. -/
theorem tensorChernRelations_chernFamily :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    TensorChernRelations r s (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX E r))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX E r))
      (homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F s))
      (homComponent 2 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F s))
      (homComponent 1
        (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * s)))
      (homComponent 2
        (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * s))) :=
  let : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
      isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
  tensorChernRelations_chernFamily_of_totalChern C sX E F _ r s (r * s)
    (tensorChernRelations_totalChern C r s sX E F)

/-- **Stacks 0FA6, the first displayed identity.** For `ℰ` and `ℱ` finite locally free of ranks
`r` and `s` on `X` locally of finite type over `S`,

  `c₁(ℰ ⊗ ℱ) = r·c₁(ℱ) + s·c₁(ℰ)`

in the ring of total Chow cohomology classes of `X`, where `c₁(-)` is the degree-one part of the
total Chern class, the first Chern class of Stacks 0B7H. -/
@[stacks 0FA6 "the first displayed identity, for every X locally of finite type over S and all \
finite locally free E and F of ranks r and s, with no further hypothesis.  The identity is read in \
the ring TotalChowClass C sX of total Chow cohomology classes, the product over p of the A^p(X) \
of Stacks 0B7E with the product of Stacks 0B75; every term of the identity is homogeneous, so it \
lies in the source's A^*(X).  c_1(E) is the degree-one part \
TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) of \
the total Chern class, the bivariant Chern class of Stacks 0B7H in degree one, and E tensor F is \
the sheaf tensor product Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor, of rank r * s"]
theorem totalChern_sheafTensor_degree_one :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * s)) =
      (r : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s) +
        (s : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) :=
  (tensorChernRelations_totalChern C r s sX E F).1

/-- **Stacks 0FA6, the second displayed identity.** For `ℰ` and `ℱ` finite locally free of ranks
`r` and `s` on `X` locally of finite type over `S`,

  `c₂(ℰ ⊗ ℱ) = r·c₂(ℱ) + s·c₂(ℰ) + C(r,2)·c₁(ℱ)² + (r·s − 1)·c₁(ℱ)·c₁(ℰ) + C(s,2)·c₁(ℰ)²`

in the ring of total Chow cohomology classes of `X`, where `c_i(-)` is the degree-`i` part of the
total Chern class, the Chern class of Stacks 0B7H. The coefficient of the cross term is
`r·s − 1`. -/
@[stacks 0FA6 "the second displayed identity, for every X locally of finite type over S and all \
finite locally free E and F of ranks r and s, with no further hypothesis, the cross-term \
coefficient being r*s - 1 as in the source.  The identity is read in the ring TotalChowClass C sX \
of total Chow cohomology classes, the product over p of the A^p(X) of Stacks 0B7E with the \
product of Stacks 0B75; every term of the identity is homogeneous, so it lies in the source's \
A^*(X).  c_i(E) is the degree-i part TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sX E r) of the \
total Chern class, the \
bivariant Chern class of Stacks 0B7H in degree i, the squares and the product are products in \
that ring, and E tensor F is the sheaf tensor product Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor, \
of rank r * s"]
theorem totalChern_sheafTensor_degree_two :
    letI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := X.ringCatSheaf) _ _ :=
        isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_tensor hE hF
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX (((sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E).obj F) (r * s)) =
      (r : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX F s) +
        (s : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 2 (totalChern C sX E r) +
        (r.choose 2 : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s) ^ 2 +
        ((r : ℤ) * s - 1) • (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX F s) *
          TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r)) +
        (s.choose 2 : ℤ) • TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sX E r) ^ 2 :=
  (tensorChernRelations_totalChern C r s sX E F).2

end Main

end Stacks.Chow

end
